#ROOMS
#2419
The Training Yard~
A square of hard-packed earth behind the armoury, walled on three sides
and open to the square through the practice ring.  A dummy stands at the
centre on a weighted post, leaning slightly, sackcloth split and resewn
along every seam.  Somebody has chalked a tally on the wall and given up
counting.

Nothing dies here.  That is the whole point of the place.  The practice
ring is underfoot where you came through it; LEAVE RING steps back out.
~
0 V 1
E
ring practice~
The ring you came in by, scuffed into the earth.  LEAVE RING takes you
back to the square.
~
E
dummy post tally~
The tally runs to four figures before the chalk gives out.  Underneath,
in a different hand: DUMMY sets it up, DUMMY REPORT tells you how you
did, LEAVE RING gets you out.
~
